  <!-- ====== PIPELINE DIAGRAM ====== -->
  <section class="mb-14">
    <p class="mono-eyebrow mb-2">// from source to execution</p>
    <h2 class="glitch mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-brand-text" data-text="The Big Picture">The Big Picture</h2>
    <p class="mb-6 text-brand-body">
      All execution models are variations on the same pipeline. The key question is <em>when</em> compilation happens and <em>how many layers</em> sit between your source code and the CPU.
    </p>

    <figure class="rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-white p-4 sm:p-6">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 800 260" class="h-auto w-full" role="img" aria-label="Source code to execution pipeline showing AOT, JIT, interpreter and Wasm paths">
        <defs>
          <marker id="rt-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
            <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="#71717A" />
          </marker>
        </defs>
        <g font-family="Inter, sans-serif" text-anchor="middle">
          <!-- Source -->
          <rect x="20" y="100" width="120" height="56" rx="9" fill="rgba(37,99,235,0.08)" stroke="#2563EB" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="80" y="124" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#18181B">Source code</text>
          <text x="80" y="142" font-size="10" fill="#71717A">.rs / .c / .py / .js</text>

          <!-- AOT path -->
          <rect x="220" y="20" width="130" height="48" rx="9" fill="rgba(22,101,58,0.10)" stroke="#16653a" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="285" y="42" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#16653a">AOT compiler</text>
          <text x="285" y="56" font-size="10" fill="#16653a">gcc, rustc, go</text>
          <line x1="140" y1="118" x2="218" y2="50" stroke="#71717A" stroke-width="1.3" marker-end="url(#rt-arrow)"/>

          <rect x="420" y="20" width="120" height="48" rx="9" fill="rgba(22,101,58,0.10)" stroke="#16653a" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="480" y="42" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#16653a">Machine code</text>
          <text x="480" y="56" font-size="10" fill="#16653a">ELF / Mach-O / PE</text>
          <line x1="350" y1="44" x2="418" y2="44" stroke="#71717A" stroke-width="1.3" marker-end="url(#rt-arrow)"/>

          <!-- JIT path -->
          <rect x="220" y="100" width="130" height="48" rx="9" fill="rgba(67,56,202,0.10)" stroke="#4338CA" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="285" y="122" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#4338CA">Bytecode + JIT</text>
          <text x="285" y="136" font-size="10" fill="#4338CA">JVM, V8, CLR</text>
          <line x1="140" y1="128" x2="218" y2="124" stroke="#71717A" stroke-width="1.3" marker-end="url(#rt-arrow)"/>

          <rect x="420" y="100" width="120" height="48" rx="9" fill="rgba(67,56,202,0.10)" stroke="#4338CA" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="480" y="122" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#4338CA">Optimised code</text>
          <text x="480" y="136" font-size="10" fill="#4338CA">at runtime</text>
          <line x1="350" y1="124" x2="418" y2="124" stroke="#71717A" stroke-width="1.3" marker-end="url(#rt-arrow)"/>

          <!-- Interpreter path -->
          <rect x="220" y="180" width="130" height="48" rx="9" fill="rgba(190,24,93,0.10)" stroke="#be185d" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="285" y="202" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#be185d">Interpreter</text>
          <text x="285" y="216" font-size="10" fill="#be185d">CPython, MRI, Bash</text>
          <line x1="140" y1="138" x2="218" y2="198" stroke="#71717A" stroke-width="1.3" marker-end="url(#rt-arrow)"/>

          <rect x="420" y="180" width="120" height="48" rx="9" fill="rgba(190,24,93,0.10)" stroke="#be185d" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="480" y="202" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#be185d">Executed live</text>
          <text x="480" y="216" font-size="10" fill="#be185d">statement by stmt</text>
          <line x1="350" y1="204" x2="418" y2="204" stroke="#71717A" stroke-width="1.3" marker-end="url(#rt-arrow)"/>

          <!-- CPU -->
          <rect x="620" y="80" width="140" height="76" rx="12" fill="rgba(16,185,129,0.12)" stroke="#10B981" stroke-width="2"/>
          <text x="690" y="108" font-size="15" font-weight="800" fill="#047857">CPU</text>
          <text x="690" y="126" font-size="10" fill="#059669">hardware execution</text>
          <text x="690" y="142" font-size="9" fill="#6B7280">x86 / ARM / RISC-V</text>

          <line x1="540" y1="44" x2="618" y2="100" stroke="#71717A" stroke-width="1.3" marker-end="url(#rt-arrow)"/>
          <line x1="540" y1="124" x2="618" y2="118" stroke="#71717A" stroke-width="1.3" marker-end="url(#rt-arrow)"/>
          <line x1="540" y1="204" x2="618" y2="140" stroke="#71717A" stroke-width="1.3" marker-end="url(#rt-arrow)"/>
        </g>
      </svg>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-brand-muted">
        AOT-compiled languages (Rust, C, Go) take the top path: everything is resolved before execution. JIT languages (Java, JS) defer optimisation to runtime. Interpreters (Python, Bash) skip compilation entirely.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>
